{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/823608-different-worlds","id":823608,"title":"Different worlds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-04T12:32:25-08:00","id":823608,"title":"Different worlds","content":"<span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I think I've finally figured out why I prefer the old world of darkness (vampire especially) to the new one. The new one should have been appealing to me - a variety of possible origin stories and histories, more links to various mythologies, more possible adventures, and no-one size-fits-all meta plot. So why do I prefer the old one so much?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">And I've figured it out. It actually *is* the metaplot. But not just the fact that there is one; the fact that it's rather good and atmospheric (sleeping monsters manipulating the world or waiting till the time is right), but because it's also vague and you can ignore it. So while the new world has a variety of &quot;choose your cool metaplot&quot; options, none of them are canonical, so none of them have depth in the story. While the old world's metaplot has depth and is intertwined with the story - but at the same time, there's so much obscurity and ambiguity about it that you can interpret it differently, OR you can just ignore it completely. So the old world has a comfy and familiar dark home with hidden crannies, that you don't have to live in, while the new world has a series of artistic but underdeveloped hotels.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">That's how I interpret it, anyway.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T05:11:03-08:00","id":825361,"title":"","content":"I see things a little bit differently.<br /> <br /> First of all, full disclaimer: this is not, in any way, an attempt to discredit cWoD over (the new) CofD. I love cWoD/oWoD. My first corebook ever was Vampire the Masquerade, and is a fact i have a soft spot for it in my heart. And i'm a total fanboy over Demon the Fallen and Werewolf the Apocalypse. So, no hate at all here.<br /> <br /> But. In cWoD the metaplot is something that affects the ongoing development of the World. That is to say, if you want to play low-tier characters, is all well and fine; as you say,you cnajust ignore it completely. You still have to acknowledge the fact of the Camarilla /Sabbat existence (for example, talking about Vampire) but well, almost nothing else. But as your characters develope their powers and grow powerful, eventually you will have to adhere, to some extent, to the metaplot, as it shapes the top tier power levels, and therefore the entire world. Of course you can just ignore it... but that is exactly what CofD is. <br /> <br /> In Vampire the Requiem, for example, there is (to some shady extent) metaplot - Rome fell by Strix among other little meaningful things here and there- and you have the Dark Eras and its stories over the history (which you can accept or forget, of course, but you have it anyway) to shape the CofD world. But the CofD &quot;metaplot&quot; is casual and forgiving enough that it will never get in the way of your game. (Even the Strix are optional). I value that freedom dearly. Besides, the sheer quality of the overall written work is amazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T01:30:33-08:00","id":825841,"title":"","content":"The metaplot in the WoD is rather blown out of proportion, though. Vampire and Mage were huge on it, but Changeling and Werewolf didn't really give a fuck, and most of the metaplot content was presented in a highly optional manner. Nor did they have as many metaplot books for that matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T02:36:51-08:00","id":825862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/823608-different-worlds?p=825841#post825841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The metaplot in the WoD is rather blown out of proportion, though. Vampire and Mage were huge on it, but Changeling and Werewolf didn't really give a fuck, and most of the metaplot content was presented in a highly optional manner. Nor did they have as many metaplot books for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Disagree for Werewolf - the eternal losing struggle against the Wyrm was a huge part of their story. But yeah, changeling and wraith were agnostic (until wraith got whacked)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T02:45:05-08:00","id":825869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheesefondue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/823608-different-worlds?p=825862#post825862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disagree for Werewolf - the eternal losing struggle against the Wyrm was a huge part of their story. But yeah, changeling and wraith were agnostic (until wraith got whacked)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not metaplot, though. That's the theme and scope of the game. There were very few metaplot books for the line, and their consequences were pretty much ignored by the game at large. I know because I have most of them :P<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T06:55:45-08:00","id":825972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/823608-different-worlds?p=825869#post825869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not metaplot, though. That's the theme and scope of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right about that, by the way. I made a mistake in my post too, speaking about the Camarilla and Sabbath. Alongside the Methuselah and the Jyhad, those elements would be also theme and scope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/823608-different-worlds?p=825869#post825869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were very few metaplot books for the line, and their consequences were pretty much ignored by the game at large.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Among many other reasons (that epic feeling ), that's why Werewolf is one of my favourites. In fact, when i talk about the dense metaplot, i'm usually thinking about Vampire.<br /> <br /> PS: Researching about the Garou i've stumbled upon one reference to Margrave Yuri Konieztko's speech in Apocalypse. Talking about epicness. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Know this, warriors of our Mother! There is nothing after this. Our ancestors have been butchered twice over, once in body and once in spirit. There is no Heaven, there will be no Hell, Valhalla does not exist. All that is will be destroyed if we fall today. And many of you will. The enemy is mighty and fearsome, and we march forward into the mouth of death. Do not fight for an afterlife reward for your bravery, for it will not come. Fight instead for Gaia. Fight for all that you know and love. Fight with every last ounce of Rage left inside you, so that even should the Wyrm destroy us, he will be awestruck by your mighty fury. Prove your arms so mighty, prove your anger so terrible, prove your love so pure and your passion so encompassing, prove your minds so resourceful and your zeal and courage so overwhelming that even should every one of us fall today, the armies of the Wyrm will never rest easy. In their reign of Oblivion, every one of their soldiers will look over their shoulders and sleep with one eye open. They will live with fear -- fear that one day, we will find a way back!</span></span>&quot; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T13:03:10-08:00","id":827727,"title":"","content":"The rpg books are like the LEGO or another construction toys, you buy the box but after you build the way you want. I love creating crazy mash-up from different franchises, for example mixing WoD and Ravenloft.<br /> <br /> In my setting the Gaia, Wyrn, Weaver and Kaos are powerful spirits, but they weren't who created the universe, they are only so powerful like the leader of a megacorporation. Wyrn doesn't destroy or taint the world but to conquest it by an army of fomoris with biopunk weapons, weaver doesn't a frozen world, but to create the web to watch de world, and kaos isn't always changing, with a primal power with enough sense of discipline and self-control to create like an atist.<br /> <br /> And I use ucronies or parallel earths, and that allows to add more supernatural creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T14:19:00-08:00","id":827782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/823608-different-worlds?p=827727#post827727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rpg books are like the LEGO or another construction toys, you buy the box but after you build the way you want. I love creating crazy mash-up from different franchises, for example mixing WoD and Ravenloft.</div> </div> </div> </div>We know. You might want to put it in your sig, so you don't have to type it up every time in every thread.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}